# Prerequisites
*.d

# Object files
*.o
*.obj

# Libraries
*.a
*.la
*.lo

# Shared objects (inc. Windows DLLs)
*.dll
*.so
*.so.*

# bison output
src/expandlabel.c
src/expandlabel.h
src/eval_expr.c
# flex output
src/parselabel.c
src/parselabel.h

# CIW autocomplete vocabulary (generated from scheduler.c by the Makefile)
src/xschem_subcommands.txt

# Action log (created at runtime in the cwd)
Xschem.log
Xschem.log.*
# ...but a log deliberately kept as issue evidence is not runtime junk (issue 0240)
!doc/claude/evidence/**

# Untitled buffers saved in the cwd (issue 0322). load_schematic() names an empty buffer
# $PWD/untitled[-n].sch (src/save.c:4407) and get_unused_untitled_name() skips numbers already
# taken (src/xinit.c:180), so a stray save from the repo root piles up one MORE file per run --
# 67 of them before anyone noticed.
#
# The /untitled.sch, /untitled-*.sch, /untitled.sym and /untitled-*.sym rules that used to sit
# here are DELIBERATELY GONE (merge 5, doc/claude/suggestions/plan_merge5_fluid_into_open_pdk.md
# section 5.6). full_audit.sh's tree_delta_snapshot() finds a suite's leaked files with
# `git status --porcelain`, which honours .gitignore -- so ignoring the leak also hid it from
# the detector, and check C37 of test_audit_classifier.tcl ("tree delta sees a leaked .sch
# FILE", issue 0353) went red on the merge. 0322's real cure is the source fix
# (get_unused_untitled_name probing the directory it is about to write into) plus the test
# hygiene in test_placement_wire_gate.tcl; the ignore rule only ever hid the residue.
# If these rules are ever restored for developer convenience, tree_delta_snapshot() must stop
# trusting .gitignore for this class first -- e.g. a second
# `git status --porcelain --ignored=matching -- ':(glob)untitled*.s[cy]*'` pass folded into the
# snapshot -- and C37's comment must say why. Do NOT instead rewrite C37 into a C39b-style
# "CANNOT see" row without filing the coverage loss against 0353.
# Their "~" autosave twins remain covered by the *~.sch / *~.sym rules below.

# Executables
*.exe
src/rawtovcd
src/xschem

/build
CMakeLists.txt
.vscode

src/Makefile
scconfig/sccbox
scconfig/configure
scconfig/config.log
scconfig/config.cache
doc/manpages/xschem.1
Makefile.conf
config.h
*.Identifier

# autosave backup files (cellName~.sch / ~.sym) -- never tracked
*~.sch
*~.sym

# headless-test scratch dirs: tests/headless/*.tcl mkdir a per-pid scratch dir
# under [pwd] (repo root) -- e.g. _nhangle_<pid>, _ase_plot_<pid>, _mkinst_<pid>.
# Tests self-clean on normal exit; crashed/interrupted dev runs orphan them here.
# Tests converted to tests/headless/scratch.tcl put theirs under .scratch/ below
# instead, and sweep dead-pid corpses from BOTH locations on the next run
# (issue 0148).
_*_[0-9]*/
tests/headless/.scratch/

# test-run DROPPINGS. A suite run from the repo root (rather than through
# full_audit.sh, which uses a temp dir) leaves its own log next to the .tcl --
# tests/headless/test_<name>.log -- plus a few older harnesses that write into
# tests/ or src/. None is an input to anything: the trustworthy record is the
# RESULT: line on stdout and, under --logdir, the action log. 32 of these had
# accumulated as untracked noise, which is exactly how a real change gets lost
# in `git status`.
tests/headless/*.log
tests/*.log
tests/*/results.log
src/*.log

# ...and the same class from run_regression.tcl, which writes each case's
# generated output next to the case rather than into a temp dir. Listed
# together because covering two of the three cases and not the third is worse
# than covering none: the odd one out reads as "this one is tracked on purpose".
tests/create_save/results/
tests/netlisting/results/
tests/open_close/results/
tests/create_save_output.txt
tests/netlisting_output.txt
tests/open_close_output.txt
